      <section class="ae-book-section" id="type">
        <p class="ae-eyebrow">03 / TYPOGRAPHY</p>
        <h2>A human voice.<br /><em>An exacting system.</em></h2>
        <div class="ae-type-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="ae-specimen-label">INSTRUMENT SERIF / REGULAR &amp; ITALIC</p>
            <p class="ae-type-display">Good technology.<br /><em>More possibility.</em></p>
            <p class="ae-type-alphabet">
              ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ<br />abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz<br />0123456789 &amp; ? !
            </p>
            <p class="ae-body-copy">
              Use for the big idea: page headlines, short statements, and moments of emphasis. Keep the lines spacious
              and the message concise.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="ae-specimen-label">GEIST / VARIABLE / 100–900</p>
            <p class="ae-type-interface">Clear thinking.<br />Useful information.</p>
            <p class="ae-type-alphabet">
              ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ<br />abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz<br />0123456789 &amp; ? !
            </p>
            <p class="ae-body-copy">
              Use for body copy, navigation, labels, and interface controls. Regular and medium weights carry most of
              the work. Keep labels small, deliberate, and readable.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
