      <section class="ae-book-section" id="system">
        <p class="ae-eyebrow">04 / THE INTERFACE LANGUAGE</p>
        <h2>Every detail<br /><em>has a job.</em></h2>
        <div class="ae-specimen-components">
          <article class="ae-component-box">
            <p class="ae-eyebrow">ACTION &amp; HIERARCHY</p>
            <h3>Make the next step clear.</h3>
            <p>Use one strong blue action per decision point. Pair it with a quieter text link or titanium outline.</p>
            <div class="ae-actions">
              <a class="ae-button ae-button-blue" href="/engineering#contact">Plan a project ↗</a><a
                class="ae-link"
                href="/engineering">Explore the studio →</a
              >
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="ae-component-box">
            <p class="ae-eyebrow">SPACING &amp; STRUCTURE</p>
            <h3>Room to understand.</h3>
            <p>
              Build on a 4px unit. Use 16–24px within components and generous 72–136px space between major sections.
              Hairline titanium borders organize rather than decorate.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="ae-component-box">
            <p class="ae-eyebrow">MOTION &amp; FEEDBACK</p>
            <h3>Quietly responsive.</h3>
            <p>
              Use brief 200–420ms transitions to clarify state. Animate opacity and small movement. Respect
              reduced-motion preferences and keep all content available before animation begins.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="ae-component-box">
            <p class="ae-eyebrow">PRODUCT ENDORSEMENT</p>
            <h3>Independent. Connected.</h3>
            <p>Use the product identity first. Keep the parent relationship visible in a footer or supporting line.</p>
            <p class="ae-specimen-label">AN ATOMA ENGINEERING PRODUCT · 2026</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ae-book-section" id="voice">
        <p class="ae-eyebrow">05 / MISSION &amp; VOICE</p>
        <h2>Say what matters.<br /><em>Mean what we say.</em></h2>
        <p class="ae-voice-mission">
          We make capable technology accessible to the people doing meaningful work. Through thoughtful design,
          transparent intelligence, and careful engineering, we help businesses and organizations move forward with
          clarity and control.
        </p>
        <div class="ae-voice-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>The vision.</h3>
            <p>
              A world where a small team can use excellent technology, understand the information behind it, and stay in
              charge of what happens next.
            </p>
            <h3>The promise.</h3>
            <p>Thoughtful engineering. Useful intelligence.</p>
            <h3>The pledge.</h3>
            <p>
              The Ethical Intelligence Project is our commitment to keep people in control, make reasoning visible,
              build for access, respect entrusted information, make AI earn its place, and stay accountable to the
              outcome.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>How we sound.</h3>
            <p>
              Calm, clear, and specific. Describe the task, who it helps, and what changes for them. Show evidence when
              it matters. Use a direct invitation when there is a useful next step.
            </p>
            <h3>Words to build with.</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>“A clearer path to the next step.”</li>
              <li>“Sources, assumptions, and questions in view.”</li>
              <li>“A website shaped around your business.”</li>
              <li>“Intelligence in service of people.”</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Keep the claims honest.</h3>
            <p>
              Use actual product capabilities, real evidence, and clearly labeled illustrations. Avoid invented
              testimonials, guarantees, performance numbers, or certifications.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

